BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 586.00 Td (If HR asked me to explain the project step by step, I would say:) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 565.50 Td (> This project was an EVE-NG airport network simulation. I wanted to show that I understand how) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 551.00 Td (enterprise networks are designed, not just how to ping between devices. I created a realistic) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 536.50 Td (airport environment with separate departments: check-in, gate, baggage, airport operations, IT) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 522.00 Td (management, guest Wi-Fi, and servers.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 504.50 Td (>) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 487.00 Td (> I started by creating a VLAN and IP plan. Each department received its own VLAN and subnet. I) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 472.50 Td (did this because different departments have different security and operational needs. For) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 458.00 Td (example, guest Wi-Fi should not be in the same network as baggage systems or internal servers.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 440.50 Td (>) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 423.00 Td (> On the switch, I created the VLANs and assigned endpoint ports as access ports. Then I) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 408.50 Td (configured the switch-to-router link as an 802.1Q trunk. I used trunking because one physical) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 394.00 Td (link needed to carry multiple VLANs to the router.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 376.50 Td (>) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 359.00 Td (> On the router, I used router-on-a-stick. That means one physical router interface is divided) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 344.50 Td (into subinterfaces, and each subinterface is tagged for a specific VLAN. Each subinterface acts) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 330.00 Td (as the default gateway for that VLAN.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 312.50 Td (>) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 295.00 Td (> I configured DHCP pools for each department so endpoints automatically received the correct IP) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 280.50 Td (address, gateway, DNS server, and domain name. I placed the DNS server in the servers VLAN and) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 266.00 Td (gave its address to clients through DHCP.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 248.50 Td (>) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 231.00 Td (> For security, I used ACLs. Guest Wi-Fi was blocked from internal airport networks, and baggage) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 216.50 Td (traffic was limited to required services like DNS and the baggage application server. I also) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 202.00 Td (configured SSH management so devices could be managed securely instead of using Telnet.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 184.50 Td (>) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 167.00 Td (> The main challenge I faced was DHCP failing on some VLANs. I troubleshot it step by step. I) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 152.50 Td (checked router interfaces, switch VLANs, trunking, DHCP pools, DHCP bindings, and ACLs. I found) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 138.00 Td (that inbound ACLs were blocking DHCP Discover traffic because DHCP clients use 0.0.0.0 before) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 123.50 Td (they receive an IP address. I fixed it by permitting UDP source port 68 to destination port 67) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 109.00 Td (near the top of the ACLs. After that, the clients received IP addresses successfully.) Tj ET
0.120 0.120 0.120 rg
BT /Helvetica 10.3 Tf 56.00 91.50 Td (>) Tj ET
